{"id": "section-body-04932", "title": "Management of Malaria in HIV and AIDS Patients", "chapterId": "chapter-five", "tocLevel": 4, "tocPath": ["APPROACH TO PATIENTS WITH EMERGENCY CONDITIONS", "MALARIA", "Management of Malaria in Special Groups", "Management of Malaria in HIV and AIDS Patients"], "blocks": [{"id": "body-04932", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Management of Malaria in HIV and AIDS Patients", "runs": [{"text": "Management"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Malaria"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "in"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "HIV"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "AIDS"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Patients"}], "level": 4, "list": {"level": 2, "numberingId": "1748"}}, {"id": "body-04933", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "If malaria is diagnosed, depending on classification of the malaria diagnosis, a full treatment with antimalarial should be given according to the malaria classification.", "runs": [{"text": "If"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "malaria"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "diagnosed,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "depending"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "on"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "classification"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "malaria"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "diagnosis,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "a"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "full"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "treatment"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "with"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "antimalarial"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "should"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "be"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "given according to the malaria classification."}]}, {"id": "body-04934", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "However, it should be noted that, clearance of parasitaemia may not necessarily be accompanied by clearance of symptoms (fever) due to the presence of other underlying opportunistic infections. HIV and AIDS infected adults with low